language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Arrange cards 1 to n on a circle so that a frog starting at card 1 and jumping k places clockwise from card k lands on every card.
given n : int(1..)
find x : matrix indexed by [int(1..n)] of int(1..n)
find pos : matrix indexed by [int(1..n)] of int(1..n)

branching on [x]

such that
$ the cards are a permutation of 1 to n, each card once
allDiff(x),
$ the frog starts on card 1, which is fixed at place 1 of the circle (this removes rotations of the same arrangement)
x[1] = 1,
$ the frog's landing places: the first is place 1, and each next place is the current card's number of places clockwise from it
pos[1] = 1,
forAll k : int(1..n-1) . (pos[k+1] = ((pos[k] - 1 + x[pos[k]]) % n) + 1),
$ the frog lands on every card, so its first n landing places are all different
allDiff(pos)
